---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import {
	APP_NAME,
	CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LEGAL_UPDATED,
	OPERATOR,
} from "../site.config";
---

<Layout title={`Privacy policy — ${APP_NAME}`} description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles your data.`}>
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6">
		<p class="label">Last updated {LEGAL_UPDATED}</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
		<article class="prose-legal mt-6">
			<p>
				{APP_NAME} is a training app operated by {OPERATOR} ("we", "us"). The short version: your workouts, body
				measurements, photos and settings are stored on your phone. Our servers get what you need to sign in, and —
				only if you are on Pro and switch on cloud sync — a copy of your training data so it can follow you to a new
				phone. Progress photos never leave your phone.
			</p>

			<h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
			<p>These are saved in a database on your device:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your profile: name, age, height, body weight, program, training experience and goal.</li>
				<li>Every workout: exercises, sets, weights, reps, times, effort ratings, notes and personal records.</li>
				<li>Body measurements (such as shoulders, waist and body fat) and goals.</li>
				<li>Progress photos. These are never uploaded, synced or included in backups.</li>
				<li>Routines, folders, favourites, gym profiles, units, timer, reminder and display settings.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Workout reminders and rest-timer alerts are local notifications scheduled by your phone. We don't collect a
				push token. The optional biometric lock uses your phone's own fingerprint or face unlock; {APP_NAME} never
				sees your fingerprint or face data.
			</p>
			<p>
				When you choose <strong>Export backup</strong> or <strong>Export spreadsheet</strong>, the file is handed to
				your phone's share sheet. Where it goes from there (Drive, email, a chat) is up to you and governed by that
				service's policy.
			</p>

			<h2>What we store on our servers</h2>
			<p>
				Sign-in is handled by Supabase. When you sign in with Google, Apple or a one-time email code, we receive and
				store:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your email address (Apple may give us a private relay address instead).</li>
				<li>Your name and profile picture URL, if your Google or Apple account shares them.</li>
				<li>A user ID, and when your account was created and last signed in.</li>
				<li>
					Technical logs the authentication service keeps for security, such as IP address and device user agent
					at sign-in.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Cloud sync (Pro, off by default)</h2>
			<p>
				If you have Pro and turn on <strong>Settings → Cloud sync</strong>, the app uploads your workouts, routines,
				custom exercises, measurements, goals, folders, gym profiles, plans, profile and settings to our Supabase
				database, linked to your account, and keeps them in step across your phones. Theme, language and the
				biometric lock stay on each phone. Progress photos are never uploaded.
			</p>
			<p>
				Synced data can only be read by your account. Turning sync off stops further uploads; the copy already on
				our servers stays until you delete your account or ask us to delete it.
			</p>

			<h2>Purchases</h2>
			<p>
				{APP_NAME} Pro is sold through Google Play. Google handles the payment; we never see your card details.
				Subscription status is managed by RevenueCat, which receives your account's user ID and the purchase details
				Google Play provides (product, price, country, dates, renewal status). We store whether your account has
				Pro and until when, so cloud sync can check it.
			</p>

			<h2>What we don't do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No advertising, and no ad or tracking SDKs in the app.</li>
				<li>No analytics on how you use the app.</li>
				<li>We never sell or rent personal data, and we don't share it except with the processors listed below.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Service providers</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Supabase</strong> — sign-in, account database and, if you turn it on, cloud sync.</li>
				<li><strong>Google</strong> — "Continue with Google" sign-in, and Google Play for purchases.</li>
				<li><strong>Apple</strong> — if you choose "Continue with Apple", to verify your identity.</li>
				<li><strong>RevenueCat</strong> — manages Pro subscription status.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
			<p>
				Account data, synced data and Pro status are kept until you delete your account. Data on your phone stays
				until you erase it in Settings, delete your account, or uninstall the app. Purchase records may be kept by
				Google Play and RevenueCat as tax and accounting law requires.
			</p>

			<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
			<p>
				In the app, go to <strong>Settings → Delete account</strong>. This removes your account and everything synced
				to it from our servers immediately, and erases all data on the phone. You can also ask us by email — see{" "}
				<a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>. Deleting your account does not cancel a Google Play
				subscription; cancel it in Google Play.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask for a copy of the data we hold, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to{" "}
				<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we'll reply within 30 days. Your training data is
				also in your hands: export it from Settings at any time.
			</p>

			<h2>Health information</h2>
			<p>
				{APP_NAME} is a training app, not a medical device. Body measurements and photos are personal; they stay on
				your phone unless you turn on cloud sync (measurements only — photos never sync), and we never use them for
				anything other than showing them back to you.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>{APP_NAME} is not meant for children under 13, and we don't knowingly create accounts for them.</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top and tell you in the app before the change applies
				to you.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				{OPERATOR} · <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
			</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
